<title>FINLAND: Finnish June construction costs rise 2.5 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Finnish June construction costs rise 2.5 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish construction costs rose 0.3 percent in June on May for a 2.5 percent year-on-year increase, Statistics Finland (SF) said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>In May, the year-on-year rise was 2.4 percent, up from 0.4 percent in April.</p>
<p>&quot;Materials prices rose 2.7 percent, the price of labour rose 3.4 percent, and prices of other input factors rose 0.5 percent,&quot; SF said of the year-on-year trend.</p>
<p>Compared to May, labour costs were up 0.3 percent, materials prices rose 0.5 percent and other input prices increased by 0.1 percent, it said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
